  "solution": {
    "text": "Difference of pressure between sea level and the top of the hill<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mtext>P</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mtext>h</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mtext>h</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mtext>Hg</mtext></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>g</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mtext>Hg</mtext></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>g</mtext></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; .......(i)<br /><br />and pressure difference due to h metres of air <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mi>air</mi></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;......(ii)<br /><br />By equating (i) and (ii) we get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mi>air</mi></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mi>Hg</mi></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mtext>h</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mtext>Hg</mtext></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mtext>air</mtext></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2500</mn><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mtext>m</mtext></math><br /><br />&there4;Height of the hill =<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>.",
